From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:20:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 069/159] net: qrtr: ns: Do not let one failed announcement
 hide the others

When a remote node says hello, announce_servers() stops at the first
service it fails to announce, so every local service after it stays
unknown to that node. When a new local service registers and the
broadcast fails, ctrl_cmd_new_server() returns before notifying the
local lookups.

On a Motorola Moto G 5G Plus (SM7250) this happened on some boots right
after the modem came up ("failed to announce new service"), and the
modem, which then never heard of a service it waits for, stalled until
its watchdog fired 65 s later ("DOG detects stalled initialization").
Every boot without the message had a clean start.

Retry a failed announcement a few times with a short delay, report the
service and error if it still fails, and carry on with the remaining
services and the local lookups.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
---
 net/qrtr/ns.c | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/qrtr/ns.c b/net/qrtr/ns.c
index bcb090ee79d4..f302f6c16d3d 100644
--- a/net/qrtr/ns.c
+++ b/net/qrtr/ns.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2020, Linaro Ltd.
  */
 
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/qrtr.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
@@ -218,24 +219,35 @@ static int announce_servers(struct sockaddr_qrtr *sq)
 	struct qrtr_server *srv;
 	struct qrtr_node *node;
 	unsigned long index;
-	int ret;
+	int ret, err = 0;
 
 	node = node_get(qrtr_ns.local_node);
 	if (!node)
 		return 0;
 
-	/* Announce the list of servers registered in this node */
+	/*
+	 * Announce the list of servers registered in this node. A remote that
+	 * has just said hello may not take the whole burst yet, so retry a
+	 * failed announcement, and never let one failure hide the servers
+	 * after it: a remote that misses a service it waits for can stall.
+	 */
 	xa_for_each(&node->servers, index, srv) {
-		ret = service_announce_new(sq, srv);
-		if (ret < 0) {
-			if (ret == -ENODEV)
-				continue;
+		int tries = 0;
 
-			pr_err("failed to announce new service\n");
-			return ret;
+		while ((ret = service_announce_new(sq, srv)) < 0 &&
+		       ret != -ENODEV && ++tries < 5)
+			msleep(20 * tries);
+
+		if (ret < 0 && ret != -ENODEV) {
+			pr_err("failed to announce service %u:%u to node %u: %d\n",
+			       srv->service, srv->instance, sq->sq_node, ret);
+			err = ret;
+		} else if (tries) {
+			pr_info("announced service %u:%u to node %u after %d retries\n",
+				srv->service, srv->instance, sq->sq_node, tries);
 		}
 	}
-	return 0;
+	return err;
 }
 
 static struct qrtr_server *server_add(unsigned int service,
@@ -487,11 +499,18 @@ static int ctrl_cmd_new_server(struct sockaddr_qrtr *from,
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	if (srv->node == qrtr_ns.local_node) {
-		ret = service_announce_new(&qrtr_ns.bcast_sq, srv);
-		if (ret < 0) {
-			pr_err("failed to announce new service\n");
-			return ret;
-		}
+		int tries = 0;
+
+		/* Retry, and still tell the local lookups below if it fails */
+		while ((ret = service_announce_new(&qrtr_ns.bcast_sq, srv)) < 0 &&
+		       ++tries < 5)
+			msleep(20 * tries);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			pr_err("failed to broadcast new service %u:%u: %d\n",
+			       service, instance, ret);
+		else if (tries)
+			pr_info("broadcast new service %u:%u after %d retries\n",
+				service, instance, tries);
 	}
 
 	/* Notify any potential lookups about the new server */
